captured
docket 0.2.0b3 (scratch install, rack-cli develop c982046f, contains P35-6 83d82b22)

Real `docket harness run --contract 1.1 --workspace <dir> --task-file <file> --model
gw/anthropic/claude-x --agent-id capture-files-1 --timeout 30 --token-file <file> --max-tokens 5000
--policy <file>` transcript, against a throwaway loopback HTTP server standing in for the model
endpoint (DOCKET_HOME in a scratch directory, DOCKET_LLM_API_KEY an obviously fake key). The
workspace was a fresh git repository. The server answered two `write` tool calls
(`greeting.txt`, then `.tack-runner/state.json`), then a final message; both paths are in
`files`, the second being the shape the adapter drops. `limits.maxTokens` echoes the 5000. The
`--policy` file was a `kind: policy` document blocking `fetch`, which docket accepted only with
`appliesTo` present (the published schema lists it as optional; docket's own validator refuses a
document without it: `missing fields: {'applies_to'}`). The scratch directory is rewritten to
`/capture` and nothing else changed.
